{"ts": "2026-11-08T08:05:00", "task": "Greedy playout for hard bots (+ three pre-existing engine bugs it exposed)", "status": "ok", "note": "choosePlayoutAction (ai/policy.ts) replaces chooseGreedyAction for hard difficulty: 1-ply score every candidate, keep the best per candidateKind (all buys share ONE kind, or 8+ market piles fill the shortlist and crowd out the explore/play lines), then roll out the rest of the turn with the same greedy policy and compare END-OF-TURN positions (ROLLOUT_MAX_STEPS=5, ROLLOUT_CANDIDATE_CAP=6). A game-winning line scores WIN_BONUS - steps (fastest win wins) and is judged by speed alone, since leftover turn pools are worthless once the game is over. Measured on First Timer (2 hard bots, seeds 1-8): the playout agrees with the 1-ply greedy on 89% of decisions, explores LESS per turn (0.24 -> 0.14) because it declines the losing fights the EXPLORE_BIAS accepted, and roughly DOUBLES the Decorations the bots win (~14 -> ~30 per game, the metric the game is decided on). Three pre-existing engine bugs the stronger AI reached, all fixed with regression tests: (1) the Kevlar Jacket ma-054o ended up in two zones at once - applyDamageWithKevlar updates state, but four call sites rebuilt the seat from the pre-kevlar player/target (restoring it into attached) or rebuilt the pile from a stale local (dropping it into no zone); reading state.mansionBottom back into the local is wrong because the reveal lives only in the local rev.mansion. (2) WE-019's bottom reveal duplicated the revealed card the same way. (3) Stale prompt options duplicated moved cards - prompts built during one action can be answered after a second prompt already moved the chosen card, so we044/ma098/ac043/we036/we037/luisDiscardOne/chooseActionCardCostAtMost and the Rebecca L1 trash-target handler now verify the source zone first (weskerDiscardOneCard and ac044Discard already did). Tests: new ai/playout.test.ts (9: legality, determinism, no mutation, fallbacks, sequencing an ammo card before the explore it enables, declining a losing explore the 1-ply bias accepts, fastest-win), +4 rulesText regressions (kevlar single/multi/trap, WE-019 bottom), bot.test.ts hard=playout, sim.test.ts explore floor 0.15 -> 0.08 plus a Decorations floor (150). Soak ~11s -> ~127s, timeout 240s. Gates: typecheck 0 (3 workspaces), server 97, client 141, client build OK, game-core 722 (36 files, incl. the soak) green."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T09:15:00", "task": "Art-only card faces in hand + resource piles", "status": "ok", "note": "CardView gains an `artOnly` prop: when the card has art, the app's printed rows (.card-top type header + cost badge, .card-name, .card-stats/.card-bonus/.card-text) and the .card::before type band are hidden (opacity 0 / display none, still in the DOM) and fade back in on :hover. Cards without art ignore the prop. Hand.tsx and the Board's resource piles pass artOnly, so those cards now show only the artwork instead of the app's name/header/cost drawn on top of a card scan that already carries its own printed name/header/cost. The HoverCard popup already shows the full card, so the details stay one hover away. ALSO FIXED: restarted the Vite dev server - its import.meta.glob is startup-evaluated and had been serving only the round-1 art set (69 of 211 PNGs), so every card from rounds 2-5 showed the placeholder frame on :5173. Verified in the browser on the prod server: all hand + resource cards carry card-art-only, .card-top/.card-name compute to opacity 0, .card::before is display:none, and the hover-reveal rules are live in the stylesheet. Gates: typecheck 0 (3 workspaces), client 142."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T12:30:00", "task": "Custom card line: MX-001 Mr. X + lobby Custom Cards toggle", "status": "ok", "note": "First fan-designed card. Ruling (Manny): 'If this infected is not defeated, place it on top of the mansion as the 5th upcoming card' = insert into the mansion DECK 5th from the top (index 4), not the bottom and not the top. New set 'custom' + game-core/src/data/custom.ts (CUSTOM_CARDS, deliberately NOT in ALL_CARDS) + InfectedEffect kind 'onNotDefeatedInsertIntoMansionAt' + mansion.insertAt(). Reachability is a room toggle: expandable Custom Cards picker in the create-room form, the host room controls and pass & play; selection rides createRoom.customCards / setCustomCards (protocol + rooms + ws) and cardsForScenario(id, {customCards}) appends them; setup() shuffles every custom mansion card it finds in that list into the Mansion (kitchen-sink scenarios exclude them from the fallback pass and append uniformly, so both paths agree). Consumed in the single-explore, multi-explore and AC-042 deferred-explore disposition paths. Art: CARD-ART/MX-001.png from Manny's scan (320x435, 256 colours, 102 KB). MA-025 was already Alliance's Duvalia, so the custom card uses the mx- prefix. Tests: engine/customCards.test.ts (13) + protocol/rooms/hotseat/Lobby cases. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 735, server 102, client 146, vite build OK. Known limitation: a not-defeated Mr. X gets no mansion-reveal overlay (it stays in the mansion zone; detectReveal only reports attached/mansionBottom/removed) - the same pre-existing gap as Uroboros Aheri's shuffle-back."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T13:10:00", "task": "Extend the mansion-reveal overlay to re-inserted cards", "status": "ok", "note": "MX-001 Mr. X (and any card that goes back INTO the mansion deck) now gets a reveal overlay. A zone diff cannot see it - the zone never changes - so detectReveal also checks the reveal itself: the revealed cards are the top exploreCount of the PRE-explore mansionDeck, and a revealed card found back in next.mansionDeck was re-inserted. Do NOT compare deck indices: every card behind the reveal shifts up, so index drift flags cards that were never revealed. Reveal.outcomeZone gains 'mansion'; App.tsx renders 'was returned to the Mansion deck.' A defeated card in the same explore still wins (the zone-change loop runs first). Browser-verified on a forced Mr. X reveal (seed 3, top of the deck): the overlay shows his art, HP 60 / ATK 30, the printed text and the new result line. Tests: +4 in anims.test.ts (client 150); typecheck clean; vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T15:20:00", "task": "Custom character line: CU-001 Ricardo Irving (L1 reveal + L2 damage bargain)", "status": "ok", "note": "Second fan card and the first custom CHARACTER (80 Health, 1 copy, level1At 3 / level2At 8). L1 revealInventoryTopForAction: during your turn, reveal the top of your Inventory; an Action there moves to your hand (once per turn, needs a non-empty Inventory). L2 damageReductionAndGiveDamage (threshold 30, reduction 10, give 10): a hit ABOVE 30 is provisionally lowered by 10 and a ricardoL2 prompt asks which Character takes 10 (options = every other seat + Decline); accepting deals 10 to the chosen Character, declining re-applies the reduction so the full hit lands. Implemented as ONE choke point, applyRicardoDamage(state, seat, hp, amount) in abilities.ts, called from EVERY applyHpLoss site (actions.ts, mercenaries.ts, nightmare.ts, outbreak.ts, skill.ts) - the engine resolves damage atomically through applyHpLoss, so a helper at that seam covers explore, traps, AoE, MA-031/037/038, Kevlar and skill damage. The two applyHpLoss calls inside the ricardoL2 prompt handler are the effect itself, not damage intake. Art: CARD-ART/CU-001.png from Manny's scan, cropped to the character art window (569x462 -> 320x260, 256 colours, 57 KB). The lobby Custom Cards picker now lists characters too (hint: Infected go to the Mansion deck, Characters enter the deal pool) and selectableCharacters(room) only offers custom characters when the room enabled them. Tests: engine/customCharacters.test.ts (11) + 2 ActionBar + 1 Lobby + 1 portrait + 1 gate case. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 746, server 102, client 155, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T17:20:00", "task": "Fan character line: LK-001 Leon, CR-001 Claire, CC-001 Claire", "status": "ok", "note": "Three more toggle-gated custom characters from Manny's scans. LK-001 Leon S. Kennedy (90 Health, L1 at 1 / L2 at 8): L1 DUAL WIELD (plusDamagePerPistolUsed amount 5 threshold 2) = +5 damage per pistol when using 2+ pistols; L2 RAPID FIRE (playAreaCardsArePistols) = every card in the play area is also labeled as a pistol. CR-001 Claire Redfield (70 Health, L1 at 0 / L2 at 7): L1 TACTICIAN (plusBuyPassive) = +1 Buy; L2 SPECIALIST (turnStartActionsForBuy) = at turn start may get +2 Actions and -2 Buy (Yes/No prompt). CC-001 Claire Redfield (90 Health, L1 at 2 / L2 at 5): L1 uses the existing ammoReqReduction with tag shotgun (-10 Ammo); L2 (healOnDefeatWithWeaponTag) = heal 5 when defeating an Infected with a Shotgun weapon. RAPID FIRE is implemented as ONE tag choke point - effectiveWeaponTags(state, seat, instanceId) in abilities.ts - and every 'is this a pistol' check reads it (exploreAmmoReq, mercenaries.weaponAmmoReq, skill.exploreSkillDamageBonus, SK-029's reveal, weaponReuse.maxWeaponUses, ammoReqForWeapon's new extraTags param). Healing is capped at max Health at each of the four defeat sites, and pendingExplore now carries weaponIds so the deferred (Las Plagas / AC-042) resolution can still apply the heal. Art: CARD-ART/LK-001.png, CR-001.png, CC-001.png from Manny's scans, cropped to the character art window. Tests: engine/fanCharacters.test.ts (28) + 4 portrait/gate cases and a Lobby case client-side. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 774, server 102, client 159, vite build OK. Browser-verified: room with the three cards selected, Leon picked as the main character - the card renders 90/90 HP with both level texts and gates, a bot drew CR-001 and shows Lv1, and both portraits load from their PNGs."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T19:00:00", "task": "Fan card line 2: CI-002 Infected Crow + FCH-008 Sherry Birkin", "status": "ok", "note": "CI-002 Infected Crow (20 Health / 10 Damage / 2 Decorations, 2 copies) has the new InfectedEffect kind onRevealRevealNextMansionCard: when revealed, reveal the next Mansion card; an Infected joins the SAME battle, anything else is shuffled back. Implemented with an infected branch in the explore handler's event-expansion loop plus a branch condition change (exploreCount > 1 || crowChainPending) so a single explore that reveals a Crow falls into that loop and the chained Infected is resolved by the existing resolveMultiExplore batch. Crows chain through each other and the loop marks expanded Crows so a re-scan cannot expand the same one twice. FCH-008 Sherry Birkin (50 Health, level1At 0, NO level2At - a single-level character) has cannotUseWeapons (passive, enforced in explore validation and enumerateLegalActions) and forceAllyExploreWithSupport (manual, once per turn). The manual ability opens a seat prompt; choosing a player immediately resolves an explore FOR them from engine/allyExplore.ts: the weapon pool is the target's hand weapons plus Sherry's, Sherry pays the Ammo (it is her turn), each weapon ends up in its OWNER's play area, defeated Infected and their Decorations go to SHERRY, the damage the Infected deals is split evenly (target rounds up, Sherry rounds down), and the exploring player redraws a fresh hand. Validation requires Sherry to afford the combined arsenal for at least one candidate target. NOTE applyRicardoDamage only COMPUTES the new Health - the caller must write it back into the seat (that bug made the first Sherry test pass silently). Tests: engine/customCrow.test.ts (8) + engine/fanSherry.test.ts (9) + 3 client cases. Art: CARD-ART/CI-002.png (whole card, like every infected PNG) and CARD-ART/FCH-008.png (character art window)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T19:12:00", "task": "Fan card line 3: EV-001 Zombie Grab + Sherry combined-ammo correction", "status": "ok", "note": "EV-001 Zombie Grab (event, 1 copy): 'Trash a weapon from your hand or discard pile; otherwise, take 20 damage, then shuffle this card into the mansion.' Per Manny's ruling the card is ALWAYS shuffled back into the Mansion (a recurring hazard). Revealing it opens a zombieGrab prompt whose options are every weapon in handAfter + discardAfterExplosives (NOT player.hand - the explore has already moved the used weapon to the play area) plus 'Take 20 damage'; the handler trashes the chosen weapon or applies applyHpLoss, then shuffleBacks the event. Custom EVENT cards needed a isCustomMansionCard predicate in setup - isMansionCard only covers the official set's types, so a custom event would otherwise never reach the deck. SHERRY CORRECTION (Manny): the forced explore may spend BOTH the exploring player's and Sherry's Ammo. resolveAllyExplore passes the combined pool to resolveExplore, then deducts Sherry's share first and the target's second; validation accepts the ability when ANY candidate target is affordable from the combined pools. Tests: engine/customZombieGrab.test.ts (6) + 1 Sherry case + 1 client case. Art: CARD-ART/EV-001.png (whole card)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T20:40:00", "task": "Bot low-HP freeze fix + mid-turn down card-destruction fix + CI-002 Crow 5 copies", "status": "ok", "note": "Three changes. (1) BOT LOW-HP FREEZE: Manny reported that once bot Health got low they stopped exploring and stopped progressing. Measured on partnersInEscape / 4 hard bots: 0 heals over 4000-action games that never ended, explores 7-38 (healthy = 60-130), seats parked at 10 HP for 600+ turns. Three coupled causes in ai/evaluate.ts, fixed together: healing items were scored at the generic 5 points so a 20g herb always lost to Ammo x10 (healItemValue now scores them at the Health they restore, 20 for healFixed20OrTrashWithSecondFor60 and 40 for healToFull/healSelfAndPartnerToFull - the Alliance 'herb' pile is the RED herb it-004, so HEAL_ITEM_KINDS + isHealingItem is the shared predicate and marketPull reads it too); HP is linear so a heal's +Health exactly cancels the gold it costs (new LOW_HP_FRACTION 0.3 / LOW_HP_PENALTY 3); and the flat -400 downed penalty made every low-HP explore look fatal, though revive sets hp = maxHp - 20 so at 10 hp a down is a +40 hp swing (downed now scores maxHp - 20 minus DOWNED_TURN_PENALTY 200, plus MAX_HP_WEIGHT 0.5 on max Health; a down at maxHp <= 20 is permanent defeat and scores -10000). Crediting the revive Health with no counterweight makes a down a HEAL - the probe then had all four seats dead within 1125 actions. Result: heals 1-3 per game, herb buys 2, explores 70-131 (was 7-38); evaluate.test.ts's 24 hardcoded expectations re-pinned from the runner's 'expected X to be Y'. (2) CARD DESTRUCTION THE MORE AGGRESSIVE BOTS EXPOSED: the soak's conservation audit failed on alliance/2 (we-023#1 and we-003#2 registered in no zone). Traced to a chooseOption on the AC-050 Resuscitate prompt: three MID-TURN down handlers set playArea: [] on the down, destroying every card in it (actions.ts resuscitate decline, mercenaries.ts dealDamageToCharacter, skill.ts damageCharacter). The normal down path (applyDownedHooks) correctly keeps the play area and endTurn discards it, so those three now keep it too; regression test in engine/downed.test.ts. Soak back to green at 22/30 natural. (3) CI-002 CROW COPIES = 5 (Manny ruling): enabling the Crow adds 5 copies to the Mansion deck; a duplicate ci-002 entry in CUSTOM_CARDS was removed. Tests: customCrow.test.ts asserts the 5-copy shape and that an enabled game has exactly 5 Crows in mansionDeck + mansionBottom. Still open (balance, not AI): the expansion scenarios cap out because they end only on Uroboros Aheri (hp 90, attack 70) and the healing supply is tiny."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T22:05:00", "task": "M6 UI: survival-horror board theme pass", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny asked to tweak the client UI, chose the board/in-game screen and the direction 'more RE atmosphere - darker, grittier, stronger horror mood'. Implemented as an override layer APPENDED to client/src/styles.css (base rules untouched) and scoped to `.app-board`, a class App.tsx now adds to the shell only in the in-game branch, so the lobby is byte-identical. Changes: (1) the room - near-black #090b0e base with a cold teal radial glow top-left, a blood-red radial glow bottom-right, a heavy vignette, and a tiled SVG feTurbulence film-grain layer at 5% opacity. (2) header + action dock are brushed-steel gradient bars with a 3px desaturated hazard-stripe edge (repeating-linear-gradient -45deg, dark gold/black); title is uppercase, 3px letterspaced, with a faint red glow. (3) board-section-title becomes a dossier heading: blood-red tick (::before) + hairline rule (::after). (4) player-panel / play-area / game-log get a darker gradient, steel border and inset top highlight. (5) buttons restyled as machined steel via `.app-board :where(button)` (zero-specificity :where so the component classes still win), with `.market-pile` and `.hand-card` explicitly reset so card-shaped buttons keep their box; Explore stays toxic green, abilities deep Umbrella purple, btn-primary blood red. (6) action-stat pills darker with thin steel borders and desaturated accents (HP #6fbf7a, gold #d4af37, ammo #7fa8c9, actions #c08a9a, buys #c99a5e). (7) card frames darkened with a heavier shadow and a darker card-back; (8) thin dark themed scrollbars for webkit + Firefox; (9) SkillPanel referenced undefined custom properties (--card, --accent, --muted-foreground) so its background/accents silently fell back - now mapped to real vars; (10) card-art scrims strengthened from rgba(8,9,12,0.72) to rgba(6,7,10,0.82) and the top scrim to 0.9 so the rules text reads on dark card art; (11) market pile captions brightened and the viewing player's panel gets a faint cold glow via [data-me=\"true\"]. Gates: client vitest 163 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean across all three workspaces, vite build OK (index css 38.72 kB). Browser-verified at 1600x1000 on a fresh pass-and-play game."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T22:20:00", "task": "M6 UI: pin the action dock to the bottom of the viewport", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'i want the action bar to be fixed to the bottom of the screen and always visible'. Measured the existing layout first: at 1600x1000, 1440x900, 1366x768, 1280x800, 1280x720, 1152x700, 1024x768 and 1024x640 the dock already sat flush at the viewport bottom (gap 0, document scrollHeight == innerHeight), so the failure is not size-dependent - it is state-dependent, when the dock GROWS (a prompt, the explore weapon picker, queued prompts). Fixed it unconditionally instead of chasing the trigger. Six edits to the base layout rules in client/src/styles.css (NOT the .app-board theme layer, since this is shell layout rather than theming): (1) .app becomes exactly one viewport - height: 100vh with a 100dvh fallback - plus overflow: hidden, so nothing inside can extend the page; (2) .app-header gets flex: 0 0 auto (flex-shrink defaulted to 1, so a tall dock could compress the header); (3) .app-main becomes flex: 1 1 auto with overflow: hidden; (4) .app-side (the 340px log sidebar) gets min-height: 0 + overflow: hidden so a long game log cannot force the row taller than the viewport; (5) .app-action-dock becomes flex: 0 0 auto with max-height: 45vh, overflow-y: auto and overscroll-behavior: contain, so a tall prompt/picker can never push it past the screen - it scrolls internally instead; (6) .board gets min-height: 0 so it is the only region that shrinks and scrolls. Verified by measurement at 1600x1000 / 1440x900 / 1366x768 / 1280x720 / 1024x768 / 1024x640 / 900x600 / 820x560: dock bottom == viewport bottom, dockGap 0, document scrollHeight == innerHeight, board scrollHeight > clientHeight (internal scroll). Stress test: injected a 900px-tall block into the dock in a 720px viewport -> dock capped at 324px (45vh), top 396 / bottom 720 so fully on screen, dockScrollsInternally true, page scrollHeight still 720, board shrank to 314px and kept scrolling. Gates: client vitest 163 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean across all three workspaces, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T22:35:00", "task": "M6 UI: remove the app header, move the status to the action bar's lower right", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'move the app status to the lower right hand corner of the action bar and remove the app header'. App.tsx: deleted the whole <header className=\"app-header\"> block (the 'RE Deck Builder' h1, the room code and the connection status). The shell is now just <main> + <footer className=\"app-action-dock\">, which also hands the board the 50px the header used to occupy. ActionBar.tsx: two new OPTIONAL props, `status: ConnectionStatus` and `roomCode: string | null`, render a `.dock-status` cluster as the last child of `.action-buttons` - the action bar's last row - pushed right with `margin-left: auto`. Optional on purpose: ~20 existing ActionBar test call sites render it without these props and a required prop would break `tsc --noEmit`. The room code moved with the status so an online room's join code is still visible in game (it stays absent in pass-and-play, where roomCode is null). styles.css: removed the now-dead `.app-header` / `.app-header h1` base rules and the `.app-board .app-header` / `.app-header h1` / `.app-room` theme rules; `.app-status` lost its `margin-left: auto` (it was the header's right-aligned child) and gained `-connecting` / `-disconnected` colours to match `-connected`; added `.dock-status { margin-left: auto; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; white-space: nowrap }`. DISCOVERY WORTH KNOWING: `.action-bar` computes to `display: block`, NOT flex - the `.app-action-dock .action-bar { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap }` rule has no effect because no rule ever sets `display: flex` on it. So the action bar is a VERTICAL STACK of full-width rows (stats row, buttons row, prompts), not a horizontal bar. That is why the status goes at the right end of the last row instead of being absolutely positioned, and why `.action-buttons` measures a full 1553px wide. Fixing the dead flex rule (or making the bar a real flex row) is a separate layout change and was NOT done here. Verified in the browser at 1600x1000: `.app-header` absent, `.dock-status` at right gap 16px / bottom gap 8px on the bottom row, right-aligned, dock height unchanged at 79px (no extra row), page scrollHeight == innerHeight. Gates: client vitest 164 passed (11 files, +1 new case for the status cluster), npm run typecheck clean, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T22:50:00", "task": "M6 UI: make the action bar a real position:fixed overlay", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'make the action bar fixed'. The dock is now genuinely `position: fixed` to the bottom of the viewport and floats over the board, instead of being a flex child that merely happened to sit at the bottom. styles.css: `.app-action-dock` gains position: fixed; left/right/bottom: 0; z-index: 50 (deliberately below the hover-card popup at 100 and the flight layer at 500 so a card preview near the bottom is never hidden behind the bar), keeping max-height: 45vh + overflow-y: auto + overscroll-behavior: contain. `.app` gains `padding-bottom: var(--dock-h, 0px)` because a fixed element is out of flow and the flex column can no longer reserve its height. App.tsx: the dock's height is measured and published as `--dock-h` using a CALLBACK REF (`ref={setDockEl}` + `useState<HTMLElement | null>(null)`) so the effect keys on the element and re-runs when the bar mounts - the dock only renders in the in-game branch (the lobby returns early), so a [] effect ran once while the dock was still absent and `--dock-h` was never set. Re-published by ResizeObserver, by a MutationObserver fallback (childList/subtree/characterData + setTimeout 0) for content changes that do not fire a resize, and on window resize. TWO REAL BUGS FOUND AND FIXED ON THE WAY. (1) `.zone-pile` had no position, so its `.zone-pile-count` badge resolved against the INITIAL CONTAINING BLOCK: it rendered at the viewport's right edge (offsetParent BODY, measured right edge 1591 vs document client width 1585) instead of on its pile, which itself sits at left 16..80. That 6px of document overflow produced a horizontal scrollbar, which made the layout viewport 15px shorter than the window (docClientH 985 vs innerHeight 1000), so `position: fixed; bottom: 0` placed the bar 15px above the physical bottom. Fix: `position: relative` on `.zone-pile`. This also fixes the badge's long-standing misplacement - it was never on the pile. (2) The measurement effect's [] dependency ran while the dock was unmounted, so the board would have scrolled underneath the bar. Verified at 1600x1000 / 1366x768 / 1280x720 / 1024x640 / 900x600 / 820x560: dock computes to position: fixed, dockBottomGap 0, dockFullyVisible true, boardHiddenPx 0, no horizontal and no vertical page scrollbar. Growth test: injecting a 300px node so the dock hits its 45vh cap moved --dock-h from 79px to 324px (and back to 79px on removal) with boardHiddenPx 0 throughout. NOTE: this headless browser reports visibilityState 'hidden', so requestAnimationFrame never fires and ResizeObserver delivery (tied to rendering steps) never fires either - the MutationObserver fallback is what makes the measurement verifiable here, and in a real visible tab the ResizeObserver covers font-load/CSS-driven height changes that mutate nothing. Gates: client vitest 164 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean across all three workspaces, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T23:20:00", "task": "M6 UI: move character/partner cards and deck/hand/discard into the action bar", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'move the player character card and partner card to the action bar in between action-stats and action-buttons; move the player's deck, hand and discard pile to the action bar to the right of the character/partner cards'. The action bar is now a real horizontal row and holds, left to right: stat pills, character + partner cards, Deck pile, hand, Discard pile, then the existing prompts/picker/buttons. IMPLEMENTATION. (1) `.app-action-dock .action-bar` gains `display: flex` - its flex-direction/align-items/gap/flex-wrap rules had been dead for the file's whole life, which is why the bar was a vertical stack of full-width rows; one declaration makes them live. (2) ActionBar renders a new `.action-identity` block between <ActionBarStats> and the prompts/buttons containing <CharacterCards>, <ZonePile Deck>, <Hand> and <ZonePile Discard>. Order verified in the DOM: player-character-row, zone-pile(Deck), hand(5 hand-cards), zone-pile(Discard). (3) New `ui/CharacterCards.tsx` holds the character + partner card pair so the action bar and PlayerPanel share one implementation; PlayerPanel gains `showCharacterCards` (default true) and Board passes `showCharacterCards={player.seat !== mySeat}`, so the viewing player's cards appear exactly once (in the bar) while every other seat still shows theirs on the board. (4) `ui/playFromHand.ts` is the hand-click to action-kind classifier moved out of Board.tsx, which no longer renders a hand. (5) Zones.tsx now renders ONLY the play area; `data-anim-zone=\"play\"` is unchanged so the card-flight layer keeps a stable target, and the moved piles keep their `deck` / `discard` anchors in the bar so flights still resolve. (6) Bar-specific sizing: the character card compacts to 100px wide, the hand to 72px cards with a -18px margin - without that the row is ~1616px and wrapped even at 1600px. ALSO: the dock-height reservation now self-corrects on a 250ms poll. A WRAP changes the bar's height with no resize event and no DOM mutation, so neither ResizeObserver nor the MutationObserver fallback sees it; the poll (guarded so it only writes when the height actually changed) keeps `--dock-h` honest, and also covers a backgrounded tab where rendering - and therefore ResizeObserver delivery - never happens. VERIFIED: 166 client tests green (+2 new: the action-bar ordering test and the showCharacterCards test), typecheck clean, vite build OK. Browser-measured at 1920/1600 the bar is ONE row (dock 157px, boardHidden 0); at 1440 and below it wraps to two rows (dock 204px, boardHidden 0); at 900 it is three rows (251px, boardHidden 0). No horizontal or vertical page scrollbar at any width from 1920x1080 down to 900x600. Board's 'Your table' now contains only the play area, and the viewing player's panel no longer carries a character card (verified: data-me=true panel has no player-character-card, the other seat's does)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T23:40:00", "task": "M6 UI: action bar as three bands, per the supplied mockup", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny sent a mockup image and said 'make it look like this'. The mockup (527x225) shows the action bar as THREE horizontal bands: (1) five stat pills BUNCHED AT THE LEFT (measured centres 0.06/0.19/0.31/0.43/0.55 of the width, right ~40% empty); (2) CHARACTER card at the far left, DECK pile at ~0.25, the hand as the wide flexible centre (~0.38-0.75) with a zoom overlay, DISCARD at ~0.92 - each of CHARACTER/DECK/DISCARD with a small uppercase label ABOVE it; (3) four buttons SPREAD ACROSS THE FULL WIDTH (centres 0.08/0.24/0.49/0.77). IMPLEMENTATION. `.app-action-dock .action-bar` switched from `flex-direction: row` to `column` and now holds three `.action-row` bands: band 1 = ActionBarStats + the phase note; band 2 = `.action-identity` with four `.action-col` columns (Character / Deck / hand / Discard), each carrying a `.action-col-label`; band 3 = `.action-row-controls` with the error toast, prompts, extra actions, explore picker/counts and `.action-buttons`. The hand lives in `.action-col-hand` (flex: 1 1 auto) > `.action-hand-scroll` (overflow-x: auto) so a large hand scrolls instead of wrapping the bar; the fan is centred with `margin-inline: auto` on `.hand` (auto margins collapse to 0 on overflow, so the cards stay reachable by scrolling). The two circular scroll buttons from the mockup sit at the hand column's top corners. `.action-buttons` is now `flex: 1 1 auto; justify-content: space-between` so the buttons spread across the band like the mockup, and `.dock-status` was lifted out of `.action-buttons` to be a sibling so it is not swept into the spread. Deck/discard piles were enlarged to 76x103 so they read as the labelled boxes in the mockup. DECLINED: the mockup's centred '100%' zoom control - Manny said 'do not add a zoom control', so no zoom state, no zoom pill and no `--hand-card-w` variable were added; the hand card width is a plain 80px. VERIFIED: 166 client tests green, typecheck clean, vite build OK. Browser-measured at 1920x1080 / 1600x1000 / 1440x900 / 1366x768 / 1280x800 / 1280x720 / 1152x700 / 1024x768 / 1024x640 / 900x600: exactly 3 bands at every size (band heights 31 / 157 / 31), dock 256px, dockFullyVisible true, boardHidden 0, and no horizontal or vertical page scrollbar. Hand confirmed centred in its column (column 220..1494, hand 702..1012)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T00:05:00", "task": "CARD ART: re-extract all 51 character cards UNCROPPED", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'pull all the character card art from this file ... do not crop the art at all', pointing at the TTS mod image httpssteamusercontentaakamaihdnetugc763858468195247095E59882E8DEA5B70A7F423CFCDF264848872A6A9A.png (40 MB, 4900x4865). That is the known character sheet: 10 cols x 5 rows @ 490x695 plus the stray bottom-left cell = 51 cards. The existing CH-*.png files were the 320x260 ART-WINDOW crop, and a side-by-side against the raw cells showed that crop was throwing away the bottom third of every illustration (Wesker's coat and gun, Kevin Ryman's vest, Rebecca's rifle and stance) plus the printed health banner and the whole name/ability text box. METHOD. Sliced the 51 cells with a 3px inset, then recovered the cell -> id mapping by TEMPLATE MATCHING rather than re-reading 51 cards with vision: downscaled each cell to 320 wide, slid the existing 320x260 CH-001 crop over every cell to find the art-window offset (y=55, matching the documented crop), then computed the full 51x51 pairwise SSD matrix between the existing crops and the cell art windows. Result: a clean BIJECTION over all 51 cells with the best match 7-20x better than the runner-up in every single case, so no vision read was needed. Saved each cell as the FULL card: LANCZOS to 320 wide (320x456), quantize(256, MEDIANCUT, FLOYDSTEINBERG), optimize=True. Total CH art went 9.3 MB -> 6.4 MB; CARD-ART as a whole is now 25 MB. The 51 previous cropped files were backed up to the Hermes scratch dir before overwriting. DISPLAY FOLLOWED THE ART: `.card-character .card-portrait` aspect-ratio 320/260 -> 320/456 (otherwise the taller image letterboxes inside the old window), and `.card.card-character` aspect-ratio 5/7 -> auto so the frame grows around the taller art instead of clipping it. Measured in the browser: the action-bar character card is now 100x169 (was 100x140) and the board panel card 140x226 (was 140x196); the dock grew 256 -> 285 px, still fully visible with 0px of board hidden and no page scrollbars. Verified the saved CH-001.png is the COMPLETE card - [CHARACTER] banner, the '100 Health' badge, the full illustration, the name/ability text box and the printed 'CC-001' number - with nothing cut at any edge. Gates: client vitest 166 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T06:55:00", "task": "LOG: make the action log public, hide only hands and inventories", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'change the way the log works in the client, in the physical game players would be able to see what the player is doing so the only things that other players shouldn't know is the contents of the other players hands and inventories'. The information model now matches a real table. CHANGED. (1) `sanitize` (game-core/src/engine/view.ts) hides ONLY another seat's `hand` and `inventory` as `hidden-N` placeholders (length preserved). The discard pile, play area, market, mansion and the ENTIRE ACTION LOG are public to every viewer including spectators. (2) The log redaction is GONE: `redactAction` used to replace another seat's `playActionCard`/`playItem`/`playAmmo` instanceId with `hidden-card` and their explore `weapons` with `hidden-wN`, which made the turn history read 'played action' with no card name for every opponent. The log is no longer transformed at all, so real card ids flow through for every seat. (3) `turnHistory.ts` now names the explore weapons too ('explored the Mansion with Handgun, Combat Knife') since they are public once used (they move to the play area). (4) `anims.ts` already skipped `hidden-*` ids, so the now-public discard/play-area cards animate for everyone with no change there. WHY IT IS SAFE: every action type that carries an instanceId moves that card OUT of the hand - playActionCard / playItem / playAmmo / playWeapon go to the play area, attachToPartner to attached, useWeaponAbility and removeAttachedItem read the play area/attached, explore's weapons go to the play area and its discardedPistols to the discard. chooseOption carries only an option INDEX, never an instance id. So no log entry can name a card that is still face-down in someone's hand or inventory. The Mercenaries draft remains the one deliberate exception (a draft hand IS a hand), so its hands/kept/pendingPass/final/deck hiding is untouched. TESTS UPDATED: view.test.ts now asserts discard/playArea stay EQUAL to the raw state for other seats, that only hand/inventory are hidden (lengths preserved, spectator too), and a new case proves a logged play keeps its real instance id when viewed from another seat; host.test.ts's sanitize integration test was rewritten to assert every viewer (0, 1 and spectator -1) sees BOTH plays with their real ids while each still sees only their own hand; testHelpers' seatHidden now checks only hand/inventory. VERIFIED in the browser on a 2-player pass-and-play game: the log reads 'T1 Player 1: played ammo Ammo x10' and 'T2 Player 2: played ammo Ammo x10' from BOTH viewpoints (before the change the other seat's line had no card name). Gates: game-core 801 passed (42 files), server 102 passed (6 files), client 166 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean. SEPARATE PRE-EXISTING BUG FOUND while verifying (NOT introduced by this change, confirmed via git): clicking a WEAPON in hand sends playActionCard, but validate requires type 'action' for that action, so the server rejects it with 'playActionCard: not an action card: we-009#s1_1' and the card never leaves the hand. The Action union has a dedicated `playWeapon` for this. playFromHand.ts still routes weapons to playActionCard, exactly as the old Board.tsx did."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T07:35:00", "task": "UI: weapon click opens the Explore picker; show other seats' public zones", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'Fix 1 and 2' — the two items flagged after the public-log commit d49ea43. FIX 1 (weapon click). Clicking a WEAPON in hand sent playActionCard, but validate requires type 'action' for that action, so the server rejected it ('playActionCard: not an action card: we-009#s1_1') and nothing happened. Checked the rulebook first (docs/rules/RE1_Rulebook.pdf, clean text layer): '(4) Exploring the Mansion — When a Character Explores the Mansion, that Player plays all of their Weapons they will be using, along with the Ammunition required'. So weapons are played AS PART OF an explore, never as a standalone action. The old route was also actively harmful: explorableWeapons() (game-core/src/engine/weaponReuse.ts) offers only hand weapons + reusable play-area weapons + partner-attached weapons, so a weapon moved to the Play Area could never be used again. ActionBar's hand onPlay now checks defForInstance(...).type === 'weapon' and, instead of dispatching, does setSelected([instanceId]) + setPickerOpen(true) — the picker opens with that weapon pre-selected. playFromHand() lost its 'weapon' case entirely and its doc comment now says why. Verified in the browser: clicking a Combat Knife opens the picker with that knife checked ([true, false]) and no error toast. FIX 2 (other seats' public zones). PlayerPanel renders, for every seat that is not the viewer, a '.player-public-zones' block: an 'In play' row with compact CardViews of that seat's playArea, and a 'Discard' row with the top card (player.discard[0]) plus an 'xN' count. Empty zones read 'none' / 'empty'. The viewer's own panel is unchanged because their Play Area already lives in the board's 'Your table' section. Verified in the browser: Player 2's panel reads 'IN PLAY none' and 'DISCARD [Ammo x10 card] x5' after their turn. LAYOUT FIX THAT FELL OUT OF IT: .player-panel had no max-width, and one long skill line made its max-content width ~1052px, which wrapped the .board-players flex row and doubled that block from 536px to 775px tall. Capped at 520px so two panels plus the gap sit side by side. Board overflow at 1600x1000 went 668px -> 471px; measured apples-to-apples the public zones themselves cost 75px (396px without them). Pre-existing board overflow of ~396px at this viewport is NOT addressed. The compact zone cards also needed 'aspect-ratio: auto' — .card is 5/7 by default, which made each 58px-wide chip 81px tall; the block was 109px before and 68px after. TESTS: +3 in client/src/ui/ui.test.tsx (169 total, was 166). playFromHand dispatches NOTHING for a weapon, and still routes action/item/ammunition to playActionCard/playItem/playAmmo. PlayerPanel renders data-public-zones for another seat (with the real card names) and not for the viewer's own panel. No DOM-interaction test framework exists (no @testing-library/react, vitest environment is 'node'), so the picker opening is verified in the browser rather than in a test. Gates: client 169 passed (11 files), npm run typecheck clean, vite build OK. game-core and server were not touched."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T08:40:00", "task": "UI: character cards match hand size, ring overlays the printed badge", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'for the player and partner cards remove the cc-head and card-name, keep health ring and overlap the one printed on the card and scale down the character card to same size as the cards in the players hand'. CHANGES. (1) CharacterCard (client/src/ui/CardView.tsx) no longer renders .cc-head (the '[CHARACTER]' banner) or .card-name (the red maroon name bar) - the CH/PR card scans already print both, so they were duplicates. (2) The HealthRing moved out of the deleted header and into .card-portrait, positioned over the Health badge printed on the art. (3) .player-character-card .card 140px -> 80px and .app-action-dock .player-character-card .card 100px -> 80px, matching .action-hand-scroll .hand-card .card. Measured in the browser: character card 80x108 vs hand card 80x112 (the small height difference is the art aspect - CH is 320x456, hand cards are 5/7). BADGE GEOMETRY: measured with a 10px-grid crop probe plus an ASCII brightness render of the top-right corner, because vision_analyze was rate-limited (429). Base CH art (whole 320x456 scan): badge centre ~(287,35), ~40px across = 12.5% of the art width. Promo art (320x292 window): badge sits higher, centre ~(287,13). Exposed as --cc-badge-x / --cc-badge-y / --cc-badge-size on .card-character with a .card-character.card-promo override. The ring is set to 18% (about 1.5x the printed badge) so it is still legible at 80px; at exactly 12.5% it was 8px and effectively invisible. Percentages resolve against .card-portrait, whose aspect-ratio matches the art, so the overlay tracks the card at any size. VERIFIED: a 10x zoom shows the green segmented ring concentric with the printed badge. HOVER POPUP FIXED AS A CONSEQUENCE: .hover-card-pop .card sets width 145px, but .player-character-card .card (line ~607) outranks it by source order at equal specificity, so the popup had silently been inheriting the on-board character-card width (140px before this change, then 80px after). Added an explicit .hover-card-pop .card.card-character { width: 200px; aspect-ratio: auto }. At ~140px the skill text broke almost every word onto its own line - skill rows measured 256px and 242px tall for a single sentence each; at 200px they are 61px and 132px and read normally. Popup now 192x392 and the ring shows the live HP number inside it. TESTS: the two assertions on the literal string 'CHARACTER' had to go (it came from the deleted banner) - CardView's character test now asserts card-skills renders and that cc-head/card-name are absent, and the PlayerPanel test asserts cc-head is absent. 169 client tests pass, typecheck clean, vite build OK. PITFALL WORTH REMEMBERING: two vision_analyze passes on the same crop disagreed (badge diameter 60 vs 40, centre y 45 vs 30), and a brightness-threshold blob detector found unrelated highlights - the ASCII brightness render was the only reliable way to read the badge position."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T11:20:00", "task": "M6 UI: mobile layout \u2014 board gets the full width, log becomes a slide-over", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'specific ui tweaks, im trying maximize board space on mobile screens'. MEASURED FIRST in the live browser at 5 viewports (2-player pass-and-play, real card data) before changing anything. At 390x844 the BOARD WAS 2px WIDE and the log sidebar took 87% of the screen; at 360x640 it was 0px. ROOT CAUSES (styles.css had ZERO @media rules): (1) .app-side { width:340px; flex-shrink:0 } cannot shrink while .board { flex:1 1 auto; min-width:auto } cannot go below its min-content width, so the board was crushed instead of the sidebar; (2) .action-identity { flex-wrap:nowrap } + .action-col-hand { min-width:160px } made the action dock 456px wide and scrollable on a 390px phone. MANNY'S CHOICES: Resource Area = one swipeable row; log = slide-over from the right, closed by default; opponents = slim chips (name / HP / star / Attached); hand cards = 64px. CHANGED (all in a new @media (max-width:820px) block + a 400px tier appended to styles.css, EVERY rule scoped to .app-board so desktop is byte-identical - re-measured 1600x1000: board 1212x730, dock 238px, sidebar 340px, unchanged): (a) Resource Area is one swipeable row - 18 piles wrapped to a column was 1072px tall at 768px and 3276px at 390px, now 159px with scroll-snap. (b) .app-side becomes position:fixed (which also removes it from the flex row, letting the board take the full width), translated 105% off-canvas until the shell carries .app-log-open, with a .app-log-backdrop scrim (tap to close) at z-index 55. App.tsx owns that class, initialises logOpen from matchMedia('(min-width: 821px)') and closes it on a change event when the window is narrowed across the breakpoint (otherwise a desktop user shrinking the window would be left staring at a scrim covering the board). (c) Opponent panels become slim chips in a swipeable row: .player-pools, .player-deck-stats, .player-public-zones, .character-skills and .player-character-row hidden, character name ellipsised. 'Attached' MOVED out of .player-deck-stats into the HP/star row in PlayerPanel.tsx - it is a score, not a deck statistic, and it is the one count the chip still shows (this also made the desktop panel 48px shorter). (d) Action dock compacted 329px -> 271px at 390x844: identity band wraps, hand gets its own full-width row at 64px, .action-buttons wraps instead of overflowing. (e) HoverCard clamps its popup centre to the viewport (half=92) - at 150-180px wide and centred on the trigger it hung off the edge of a phone. (f) .lobby-form wraps: the join form was 532px in a 358px container, which forced the phone to widen the layout viewport to 548px; fixed with flex-wrap:wrap + input{flex:0 1 220px;min-width:0}. LATENT BUG EXPOSED: .board is a flex COLUMN with overflow:auto, so its sections defaulted to flex-shrink:1 and were squeezed instead of the board scrolling - at 360x640 the players block collapsed to 4px. Fixed with .app-board .board > * { flex: 0 0 auto }. MEASURED AFTER: 390x844 board 374x557 (was 2x483), dock 271px/32% (was 329px/39%), market 159px (was 3276px), no board scroll, no page overflow. 360x800, 414x896, 430x932 and 768x1024 also fit with no scrolling. 360x640 (a 2014-era screen) still scrolls ~160px - the dock alone is 48% of that viewport. TESTS: the client suite is renderToStaticMarkup in a node env, so none of this is covered by it; every number above is from the live browser (interactions verified too: log button opens the slide-over, scrim and X close it, market row scrolls to scrollLeft 468). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), client 169, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T14:10:00", "task": "UI: declutter the action bar \u2014 borderless character art, attached badge, tighter stat pills", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: four action-bar tweaks. (1) REMOVED .action-col-label (CHARACTER/DECK/DISCARD captions) - the character card needs no caption and the deck/discard ZonePiles carry their own .zone-pile-label, so nothing is lost. (2) CHARACTER CARDS NOW USE THE ART-ONLY FACE like the resource piles: CardView forwards artOnly to CharacterCard which adds card-art-only; .card.card-character.card-art-only drops the 3px frame, the corner ticks and the 4px inset so the art fills the card edge to edge. The card needs an EXPLICIT aspect ratio because the portrait becomes position:absolute and no longer gives it height (320/456 base, 320/292 promo). The live HP ring still lands on the Health badge printed in the art. Measured 1600x1000: char card 80x114 border 0 padding 0 transparent bg no shadow vs hand card 80x112 border 0 padding 0. PITFALL: .card.card-character is defined AFTER the art-only block and also has two classes, so the override MUST be .card.card-character.card-art-only (3 classes) or border/padding silently lose to source order - this was caught in the browser, not by tsc. Manny was asked which he meant (frame removed vs hover popup resized vs rules panel revealed on hover) and chose 'the card itself loses its 3px frame and the art fills the whole card'. (3) PARTNER CARD RENDERS IDENTICALLY TO THE PLAYER CARD: the 'HP x/y' and 'Attached N' spans under it are gone; the attached count is a .cc-attached badge in the visual language of a .zone-pile-count (gold disc, right/bottom -5px, bottom-right) on BOTH cards so the pair stays identical. Verified in a real partner-mode server room: both 80x114, same class list, same single .card-portrait child, no player-partner-* spans, badges 18x18 reading 0. (4) STAT PILLS 25% SMALLER AND BORDERLESS: base font 11->8.25px, strong 14->10.5px, padding 4px 10px->3px 7.5px, gap 4->3px, border none; .app-board override font 10->7.5px, strong 15->11.25px, padding 4px 12px->3px 9px, border none; the mobile tiers now only tighten padding so they inherit the already-shrunk values. TESTS: +3 in ui.test.tsx (172 total) - character artOnly gets card-art-only/data-art-only, plus a new CharacterCards describe asserting both cards render the same with no text underneath and that the badge carries the right counts. FIXTURE PITFALL: the partner fixture must register the partner CHARACTER instance in state.cards as well as partnerInstanceId, or defForInstance returns null and only the main card renders. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), client 172, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T16:40:00", "task": "UI: character cards enlarge in place on hover, rules text over the art", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'remove all current hover card implementations on character cards, when a character card is hovered on, it should get larger, have its card text rendered overlayed on the card art like the resource cards behave'. DONE: CharacterCards no longer wraps either card in HoverCard, and the dead .hover-card-pop .card-character* sizing rules are deleted. Instead hovering a character card now scales the card itself 2x (transform, so the bar never reflows) and fades its rules panel in OVER the art on a rgba(8,9,12,0.78) scrim - the same reveal a resource card gives its printed rows. THREE MEASURED FACTS THAT TOOK ITERATION: (1) transform-origin must be BOTTOM LEFT. The card is the leftmost control in the bar; with 'center bottom' the 2x card measured x=-24 at 1600x1000, i.e. off the left edge of the screen. (2) The rules panel must be absolutely positioned (so it never changes the card's size), rendered with pointer-events:none while invisible (it overflows the card and otherwise swallows clicks on the deck/hand control above it), the skill rows must stack the stat box ABOVE the text (side-by-side leaves ~38px = one or two words per line), and each level's text must be clamped to 3 lines like .card-has-art .card-text. Unclamped, the panel measures 161px for Barry on a 114px card and 175px for Rebecca on a 73px PROMO card - it can never fit; at the inherited 8px font it clips the second level entirely, 6px fits. (3) The dock was clipping the enlarged card at its top edge (overflow-y:auto), so .app-action-dock:has(.player-character-card:hover) { overflow: visible } - scoped to the hover, so the dock still scrolls normally otherwise. PHONE (<=820px): the card is only 44-56px wide / 63-79px tall, so the overlay is smaller (5px, 2-line clamp) and max-height:none; the panel runs ~8px past the card onto the hand row below it, inside the dock. VERIFICATION PITFALL WORTH REMEMBERING: headless Chrome never advances CSS transitions - they stay 'running' at their start value, so getComputedStyle reports an identity transform and opacity 0 during a hover and the feature looks broken. Inject 'transition: none !important' before measuring, and confirm the selector with el.matches(':hover') / document.querySelector('.player-character-card:hover .card'). MEASURED AFTER (live board): desktop card 160x228 / panel 160x182, tablet 112x160 / 112x142, phone 88x125 / 88x142 - panel.scrollHeight == clientHeight at every size (no clipping), panel opacity 1, dockOverflow visible, no page overflow, no board regression. Tests unchanged at 172 (no test asserted the character popup). Gates: typecheck clean, client 172, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T18:05:00", "task": "UI: fan a character's attached infected out beside it on hover", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'for the character card hovercards, also display attached cards to the right of the character, the overlays the character card + attached cards similar to the way the hand is displayed, increase the card overlap proportional to the number of attached cards'. DONE: CharacterCards resolves player.attached / player.partnerAttached to defs and renders them as art-only CardViews inside .cc-attached-fan (one fan per character). The hover transform moved from .card to a new .cc-fan wrapper so the trophies enlarge together with the character card at the same scale; .cc-fan is position:relative and the fan is position:absolute at left:100%, so revealing it never reflows the action bar and it starts flush at the character card's right edge. OVERLAP: a FRACTION of the card width, --cc-overlap, computed from the trophy count by the exported attachedOverlap(count) - 0.25 at one trophy (matching the hand's own 25-30%), +0.08 per extra trophy, capped at 0.85 so cards never stack backwards. CSS: margin-left: calc(var(--cc-overlap) * var(--cc-w) * -1) on every fan card except the first. REFACTOR REQUIRED: the card width moved to --cc-w on .player-character-card (80px, 56px <=820px, 44px <=400px) instead of being set directly on .card, so the fan sizes itself identically. Three existing rules changed: '.player-character-card .card', '.app-action-dock .player-character-card .card', and the two mobile width overrides. MEASURED LIVE with 5 trophies injected (temporary window.__store probe in store.ts, removed afterwards via git checkout): desktop character 160x228 with a 448px fan starting flush at its right edge; mobile 88x125 with a 247px fan ending 47px INSIDE the dock. No page overflow, board does not scroll, rules panel still fits. --cc-overlap read 0.55 for 5 trophies (0.15 + 0.08*5) exactly as designed. TEST LESSON: the older assertions html.match(/card-character/g).length === 2 and /cc-attached/g === 2 broke because the fan adds card-art-only and cc-attached-fan elements. They now match the full class (/card card-character/g) and class=\"cc-attached\" instead of a bare substring. +2 tests: fan markup present, and overlap grows with the count and is capped. Gates: typecheck clean, client 174, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T18:40:00", "task": "UI: bigger ability text, Lv1:star stat boxes, floating controls band", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny asked for three more UI changes on top of the character hover work. DONE: (1) ABILITY TEXT SCALED - the overlay was 6px, now 7px desktop / 6px mobile. 7px is the largest size whose two clamped rows still fit the 114px base card (content 91px; 8px needs 121px and clips). Promo cards use the short 320x292 art window (73px tall) so they clamp to 2 lines instead of 3. (2) STAT BOX READS 'Lv1:\u2605' / 'Lv1:\u2606' - replaced the pixel SkillIcon glyph, the .skill-level span and the .skill-gate number with one string Lv{level}:{star}. SkillIcon deleted from CardView.tsx along with its CSS and the .card-character .skill-level/.skill-gate rules. The absolute decoration gate is NO LONGER DISPLAYED - it moved into the box's title tooltip and stays on the panel as data-level1-at / data-level2-at. Locked rows keep opacity 0.55 so inactive skill text stays greyed until unlocked. TEST CHURN: 7 assertion blocks asserted the gate number (>0<, >4<, ...); they now assert the star text plus data-levelN-at, so the gate thresholds are still covered. (3) CONTROLS BAND FLOATS - .app-action-dock .action-row-controls is now position:fixed; left/right:0; bottom:var(--dock-h,0px); background:transparent; border:none with its own padding. It stays a DOM child of the dock so the .app-action-dock overrides keep applying, and is anchored to the dock height App.tsx publishes as --dock-h so it follows the dock when it wraps. Mobile carries padding 0 8px 6px since it is no longer inside the dock. MEASURED at 1280x800: band y=590..629 (39px), dock starts at y=629 (they touch exactly), band overlaps the board's bottom 23px; no page overflow. The dock shrank 213px -> 171px. NOTE: the board still scrolls on desktop (content 1438px in a 597px box, mostly the 531px .market-piles block wrapping into rows) - PRE-EXISTING, not caused by these changes. Gates: typecheck clean, client 174, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T15:20:00", "task": "UI: every character card is 80x114 (promo art letterboxed)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'increase the size of the player character card to be 80x114 to match the partner character card'. ROOT CAUSE: promo characters (set='promo' - pr-001 Chris, pr-002 Jill, pr-009 Rebecca, pr-010 HUNK) have a shorter art window, and the rule '.card.card-character.card-promo.card-art-only { aspect-ratio: 320/292 }' made their cards 80x73 while base characters were 80x114. In partner mode the main and partner are drawn independently, so a seat could end up promo-main / base-partner. Confirmed with a live ws probe: seat 1 = Jill Valentine (Promo) / Chris Redfield (premier). FIX: removed the promo aspect override so EVERY character card is 320x456 = 80x114 at --cc-w: 80px. Promo art is LETTERBOXED, not stretched or cropped - cropping (object-fit: cover) would cut off the printed Health badge near the right edge, and the live HP ring's --cc-badge-x/y percentages resolve against .card-portrait, so the portrait keeps aspect-ratio: 320/292 and is centred vertically (top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%)) with the card's own gradient filling the letterbox. That keeps the ring exactly on the printed badge. Also dropped the promo-specific two-line skill clamp since the card is full height now. VERIFIED LIVE in a real 2-player Partner Mode room (throwaway ws probe hosted the room, browser joined as the second player and started the game): every seat's main AND partner card measured 80x114; the promo portrait measured 80x73 centred with 20px above and 21px below; the HP ring sat on the art's top-right badge; hovering the promo card scaled it to 160x228 with the portrait at 146px and the rules panel fitting (scrollHeight == clientHeight, 93px), boxes reading Lv1:\u2606 / Lv2:\u2606. TOOL NOTE: to reproduce, host a room with a raw ws client (createRoom partnerMode:true, joinRoom, selectSeat, startGame) and let the browser join the printed room code as the second player. Input.dispatchMouseEvent can time out on a busy board - set a taller viewport (1280x1250) so the action bar is on-screen, then use click_at_xy. Gates: typecheck clean, client 174, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T15:45:00", "task": "UI: turn, total-decoration, room and status chips in the stats bar", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'add the turn count and total player decoration count to the action-stats bar, move the room number and status to the action-stats bar as well'. DONE: ActionBarStats gained four OPTIONAL props (turn, decorations, roomCode, status) and renders four more .action-stat chips after Buys: 'Turn N', the decoration total, 'Room CODE' and the status word. Optional so the existing five-chip call sites and tests still work. 'TOTAL PLAYER DECORATION COUNT' = sum across every seat (state.seats.reduce((sum, s) => sum + s.decorations, 0)) - it sits next to the game-level turn counter, not the viewing player's per-turn numbers. Test builds a 6 + 4 state and asserts the chip reads 10, not 6. REMOVED the .dock-status corner group from ActionBar plus its CSS and the mobile .app-room / .app-status / .dock-status leftovers. The chips keep the app-room / app-status app-status-<s> classes and data-app-status so existing test hooks still work; the ActionBar test now also asserts they appear after 'action-stats' in the markup and that 'dock-status' is absent. CSS SPECIFICITY GOTCHA: '.app-board .action-stat' (two classes, later in the file) paints every chip neutral grey #7f8896; a two-class '.action-stat-status.app-status-connected' TIED with it and lost on source order, so the connection colour silently never applied. The status colour rules are now THREE classes. The status chip's <strong> is 'color: inherit' so it takes the chip colour. Also: the status chip holds only a value, so without a <strong> its line box was 14px against the other chips' 19px - wrapping the value in <strong> makes all chips the same height. MEASURED: desktop 8 chips in one row, all 22px tall, status green rgb(123,216,143); mobile 8 chips over two rows, all 19px tall, dock 234px, no dock scroll, no page overflow. Gates: typecheck clean, client 178, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T16:10:00", "task": "UI: own board panel removed, hover text unclamped, hover card on top", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny asked for three things: remove the player's player-panel from board-players, make the character card hover scale large enough for ALL ability text to render, and make the character + partner hover card display over all other UI. 1) BOARD: Board.tsx now renders PlayerPanel only for player.seat !== mySeat. The viewing player's panel was pure duplication (the action bar already shows their cards, HP, decorations, resources, deck, discard) and was the tallest block on the board. Board height at 1280x900 went 597 -> 697. PlayerPanel's isMe prop remains for compatibility but is now always false from the board. 2) UNCLAMPED PANEL: it had -webkit-line-clamp:3 per level and max-height:100% of the card. Measured content heights at 7px in an 80px card (card is 114px): Leon/Claire/Barry/Ada/Krauser fit (102-111), but Wesker 166, Chris promo 157, Jill promo 140, Rebecca Nurse 229, HUNK 239. Removed the clamp and the card-height cap, made .skill-text a plain block, and gave the art-only card overflow:visible on hover so the panel can extend past the card's top. Safety cap is now calc((100vh - 40px) / var(--cc-scale, 2.5)) - THE DIVISION IS REQUIRED because max-height applies in pre-transform units, so without it the rendered cap would be 2.5x the viewport. Mobile 2-line clamp removed too. 3) SCALE 2 -> 2.5 via a new --cc-scale custom property on .player-character-card, and stacking fixed: .player-character-card:hover z-index 40 -> 60, plus new .app-action-dock:has(.player-character-card:hover) { z-index: 80 } which lifts the WHOLE dock above the log slide-over (60) and scrim (55). Raising only the card's z-index CANNOT work - the dock is a stacking context, so a child can never escape its siblings' z-indexes. Panel background 0.78 -> 0.92 alpha because at 0.78 covered buttons bled through and looked like they were on top. VERIFIED: Wesker renders both rows with scrollHeight == clientHeight (166px, clipped false); a synthetic HUNK worst case renders 239px unclipped at 2.5x. elementFromPoint at a point inside both the panel and the EXPLORE button returns .skill-text (panel on top); same against the open log (dock 80 > log 60 > scrim 55). Mobile 390x844: card 110x157, panel 110x577 inside the viewport. Desktop 1280x900: card 200x285, panel 200x415. TEST: the Board test now expects 1 panel (not 2), no data-me=\"true\", and data-seat=\"1\". Gates: typecheck clean, client 178, game-core 801, server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T17:35:00", "task": "Unofficial Expansion 1: EX-001..EX-009 custom card line", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny supplied a 3x3 sheet of nine fan cards. Transcribed with the LOCAL Ollama vision model (SetneufPT/Gemma4-12B-IT-QAT_Q4_64K_16GB-GPU, vision-capable) because vision_analyze was 429-rate-limited all session; printed codes read from per-card bottom-right corner crops (full-card reads pattern-completed the numbers). RULINGS (Manny): [STORAGE]/[BOX] are mansion TOKENS; EX-002's printed text is WRONG - corrected to 'when gained attach it to your character. the next time an infected with 80 or more health is revealed while exploring, defeat it immediately and remove this card from the game' (80 = the INFECTED's Health, not the Character's); EX-005 grants +50 Ammo AND +50 Gold; EX-007 returns to its OWN market pile; EX-009 is a new 'counter' type in a shared board supply that returns there when the Character dies. Copies: 2 each for the two Infected, 1 each otherwise (copies question skipped - implemented default). 'Conditions' maps to Decorations. BUILT: CardType 'counter' + CardZone 'supply' + PlayerState.counters + GameState.supply + CardDef.counterEffects; engine/counters.ts; new effect kinds gainCardAndRemoveToken / gainAnyWeaponAndRemoveToken / attachOnGainDefeatInfectedAtOrAboveHp / onNotDefeatedAttachCounter / returnToMarketAndRemoveCounters / damageAtTurnStart. Custom MARKET cards are NEW plumbing: pilesForScenario(id,{customCards}) gives every selected custom card that prints a cost its own custom-<id> pile (EX-002/005/007); cardsForScenario pulls in a referenced counter (EX-006/008 -> EX-009); setup() seeds the supply. EX-002 attaches in gainCard and fires from BOTH explore paths (single overrides the outcome; multi filters the auto-defeated Infected out of the batch and still awards its trophy/Decorations). EX-006/008 attach in single, multi AND both pendingExplore resolvers, max one per Character. EX-009 damages at the very top of startTurnInternal before the downed check (lethal = down + turn ends); death returns it to the supply. EX-007 returns to its home pile. PITFALL THE SOAK CAUGHT: a single-card pile is EMPTY once bought, so scanning for a surviving copy orphaned the herb in NO zone - the lookup now falls back to the custom-<id> convention and removes the card if there is no home pile (never orphans). BONUS FIX: the log said 'bought (custom-ex-007)' for single-card piles - Action.buy now carries an optional instanceId, the buy handler writes the physical card onto the log entry and turnHistory prefers it. UI: typeLabel/typeClass gained counter/event/skill; PlayerPanel renders a data-player-counters row; Board renders a Counter supply pile; lobby hint updated. Art: CARD-ART/EX-001..EX-009.png sliced from the sheet (3x3, even division + 3px inset, quantized). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 821, server 102, client 171, vite build OK. engine/unofficialExpansion.test.ts (20 tests) covers every card + a 3-seed full bot game asserting conservation and counter cycling. Browser-verified on the prod server: picker lists all 9, the 3 new piles render with art, the Counter supply renders, a buy logs the card name, an explore resolves. Still open: the ally-explore path does not apply EX-002/006/008 effects; counters live only on the MAIN Character; EX-002 is buyable at 130 as well as granted by EX-001."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T19:20:00", "task": "Partner leveling from Main Decorations + bots leading explores with the Partner", "status": "ok", "note": "Two fixes Manny asked for after auditing partner mode. (1) The Partner never leveled: PlayerState had no partner level, nothing in engine/ resolved the partner's own card def, and CharacterCards.tsx hard-coded decorations={0}. Added partnerAbilities(state, seat) in engine/abilities.ts which derives the level on the fly from levelForDecorations(def.level1At, def.level2At, player.decorations) per the Alliance rulebook ('Your Partner's level is determined by the total Decorations attached to your Main Character'); the partner CardView now gets player.decorations so its badge and skill gating advance. (2) Bots never led with the Partner: enumerate.ts emitted explores with no leader so exploreLeader always fell back to 'main'. enumerate now emits BOTH leaders when the seat has a partner. Because the leader is the one fighting, its abilities must apply: new leaderAbilities(state, seat, leader) resolver wired through the explore path (actions.ts abilities/requiredAmmoForExplore/exploreAmmoReq/davidAbilities/ricardoReduction/defeat prompts/damageRedirectToPartner) and validateExplore (cannotUseWeapons, singleWeaponLimiter, weaponCostCap, ammo); exploreDamage/requiredAmmoForWeapons/requiredAmmoForExplore/exploreAmmoReq gained optional ability/leader params so every pre-partner call site is unchanged; the client explore picker + ActionBar pass the selected leader so the preview prices the leader and legality is per-leader. KNOWN BOUNDARY (deliberate): partner abilities fire only when it LEADS an explore; turn-start heals / attach caps / manual abilities still read the Main's, and useCharacterAbility still indexes the Main's ability list. Tests: game-core 828 (was 821, +7 engine/partnerLevel.test.ts), client 182 (was 181, +1 leader-priced preview), server 102. Gates: typecheck clean, vite build OK, soak ~235s unchanged."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T20:20:00", "task": "Partner as a full second character (abilities) + bots heal their Partner", "status": "ok", "note": "Four pieces. (1) seatAbilities(state, seat) unions the Main's and Partner's abilities (a seat shares one hand/discard/inventory, and the Partner is 'another Character under your control'), with a PER_CHARACTER_ONLY exclusion set (cannotUseWeapons, singleWeaponLimiter, weaponCostCap, noHealingNoNonInfectedAttach, setHpToOnLethal, infectedDamageReduction, weaponDamageReduction, damageReductionForAmmo, exploreDamageReductionPerHandCard) so one character's personal limits never leak onto the other. Routed the player-scoped consumers through it (validate hasAbilityKind, mercenaries weaponAmmoReq, and 14 sites in actions.ts). Test caught a bug: the early return when the Main has no abilities skipped the exclusion filter. (2) Turn start reads seatAbilities for the 'may' prompts and the infection/Excella draws, looks each prompt's text up from the owning character, and the Partner's healAtTurnStart now restores partnerHp (Steve L1) instead of the Main's. (3) useCharacterAbility gained character?: 'main'|'partner' with characterSource() resolving def+level; enumerate emits both characters' abilities; ActionBar labels the Partner's with 'Partner: ' (data-ability-character); Steve's L2 self-heal targets partnerHp when the Partner owns it. (4) Healing reaches the Partner: the old playItem computed healPartner and never used it; First Aid Spray, Green Herb (Heal 20 and Heal 60 paths) and Red Herb now heal BOTH characters. DESIGN DECISION FLAGGED: healing items help the whole team rather than a chosen target (the Red Herb effect was already named healSelfAndPartnerToFull and actions.test.ts's fixture text was always 'heal yourself and your partner to full Health'; the data file's '+20 max HP' text was wrong and was fixed). Bots: the First Aid Spray has no prompt, so the 1-ply evaluation sees the restored Health and the bot plays it when the Partner is hurt; evaluate.ts already scored partnerHp. Tests: game-core 16 in engine/partnerLevel.test.ts (+9), client 183 (+1 partner ability button). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), server 102, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T20:40:00", "task": "Healing items target one character (Red Herb heals both)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny's ruling: only the Red Herb heals both the Main and the Partner at once; every other healing item needs a specific character as its target. playItem gained healTarget?: 'main' | 'partner'. healToFull (First Aid Spray) and healFixed20OrTrashWithSecondFor60 (Green Herb) heal exactly the named character; healSelfAndPartnerToFull (Red Herb) still heals both and ignores the target. When a partner is alive and no target is named, the engine asks first: a new 'healTarget' prompt (['Heal Main','Heal Partner']) for the spray, and the Green Herb's existing 'healGreenHerb' prompt grows target-qualified options (Heal Main 20 / Heal Partner 20 / ... ), decoded back into (target, amount) from the option index; with no partner the labels stay the plain 'Heal 20'/'Heal 60' the existing tests assert. Naming the target applies the heal immediately instead of raising a prompt, which is what lets the bot aim one. enumerate emits both targets for the bot when a partner is alive. characterCannotBeHealed now checks the TARGET character, so Chris as the Main can still heal his Partner (and a Partner who is Chris cannot be targeted). The data file's Red Herb text ('+20 max HP') contradicted its own effect and was fixed to 'Trash with a Green Herb: heal yourself and your Partner to full Health.' Bots: the First Aid Spray has no prompt so the 1-ply evaluation sees the restored Health and the bot plays it at the Partner; a test asserts the bot picks healTarget 'partner' when the Main is already at full Health. Tests: game-core 838 (was 837; 17 in engine/partnerLevel.test.ts), client 183, server 102. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T02:20:00", "task": "Promo (PR-*) card art re-extracted as whole cards from the TTS promo sheet", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny supplied the promo contact sheet (5500x5390, cards filling only the top 1539 px: 10 @ 550x770 in row 1 plus the stray CH-022 Kevin Ryman below) and asked for the promo character cards to be pulled from it, replacing the cropped images in use. The existing PR-*.png were the 320x292 ART-WINDOW crops (portrait only, no name banner or ability text) - the last holdout after the regular CH art went full-card. All ten are now the WHOLE CARD SCAN at 320x448 (the 550x770 cell), quantized to 256 colours, ~101-114 KB each. Cell-to-code mapping was confirmed by pixel-matching the old crops against the new cells (mean abs diff 4.4-7.5 for the true match vs 33-74 otherwise) and cross-checked with bottom-right corner OCR; the OCR misread r0c8 as PR-001 (it is PR-002), so the pixel match is authoritative. Mapping: PR-001<-r0c5, PR-002<-r0c8, PR-003<-r0c7, PR-004<-r0c9, PR-005<-r0c3, PR-006<-r0c0, PR-007<-r0c4, PR-008<-r0c6, PR-009<-r0c1, PR-010<-r0c2. The stray CH-022 was skipped as a duplicate. CSS: .card-character.card-promo .card-portrait (and the art-only variant) moved from aspect-ratio 320/292 to 320/448, and the promo health-ring badge from (89.5%,4.5%) to (89.7%,6.7%) after measuring the PR-001 badge against the known-good CH-001 badge in the same crop. Verified in the browser: the promo card renders the complete card (banner, art, name, both abilities) with the ring concentric on the printed badge, and the img box (54x76.4) sits inside the card (56x79.8) with object-fit contain so nothing is clipped. PR-003..PR-008 still have no engine CardDef but their art is kept as before."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T03:05:00", "task": "Unofficial Expansion 1 art re-pulled from Manny's updated EX sheet (+ separate EX-002 card)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny sent a new EX sheet (840x1216 PNG) and asked for EX-001..EX-009 to be pulled from it. It is a 3x3 grid whose top-middle slot is EMPTY (pure white, std 0) - that is EX-002's slot, so the sheet carries only 8 cards. He then sent the EX-002 Special Rocket Launcher card separately (1054x1492 PNG, card face only, no background) and said to use it for EX-002. Mapping: EX-001<-r0c0, EX-003<-r0c2, EX-004<-r1c0, EX-005<-r1c1, EX-006<-r1c2, EX-007<-r2c0, EX-008<-r2c1, EX-009<-r2c2, confirmed by reading each bottom-right corner crop individually (a full-sheet read mislabelled r0c2 as EX-002; the name 'Weapon Case' is EX-003, EX-002 is the Special Rocket Launcher weapon card). Grid boundaries were the tricky part: the strong dark peaks in the edge-strength profile are the cards' OWN frames, not gutters - the real gutters/margins are only 1-2px. The reliable anchors are the white empty slot (x 283..558) and the black outer margins (x 0, 833..839, y 0, 1214..1215). Correct card rectangles: col1 x 1..282, col2 x 283..558, col3 x 559..832; row1 y 1..404, row2 y 414..810, row3 y 813..1215. The first attempt used the dark peaks as gutters and cut 4-5px into every card. All nine are quantized to 256 colours at ~274-282 px wide (EX-002 downscaled from 1054 to 282 to match the set), tight to the card's decorative frame with no white border - matching the rest of CARD-ART (MA-001/WE-001/AC-001/IT-002 all measure 0% white border); the OLD EX art was the anomaly, carrying a few px of blank card base outside the frame. The new renders differ from the old artwork (resize-and-diff 64-89 mean abs), so these are genuinely new images. Verified: vite build emits all nine hashed assets and :1724 serves them (EX-002 91489 B, EX-009 86579 B)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T03:35:00", "task": "Fix: partner death left the explore leader stuck on 'partner', blocking every explore", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny reported that after his Partner died while LEADING an explore (Six Shooter + Knife attached), the following turn he could not explore at all. Two defects found. 1) CLIENT (the blocker): ActionBar's `leader` is component state and was never reset when the Partner died. The leader toggle hides itself once partnerInstanceId is undefined but the state survived, so every later explore was priced with leaderAbilities(state, seat, 'partner') (which returns [] for a dead Partner) and the action was sent as leader:'partner', which validate rejects with 'explore: no partner'; the picker also evaluated the combo against (e.leader ?? 'main') === 'partner' so combo.legal was false and the Explore button rendered disabled. Fixed with a pure helper resolveExploreLeader(state, seat, leader) in client/src/ui/explorePicker.ts that falls back to 'main' when the seat has no partner, used for the weapon options, the preview and the action, plus an effect that resets the state. The engine was never at fault: explore already falls back to the Main when partnerLeading is unset, and enumerate only offers the Main once the Partner is gone. 2) ENGINE (spec violation, not the blocker): docs/rules/ALLIANCE-ENGINE-SPEC.md (3) PARTNER DEATH says a Partner at <=0 HP is removed from the game permanently and all cards attached to it are trashed. The death branch only cleared partnerAttached, so the attached cards vanished from the player state while still sitting in state.cards. Both death sites in actions.ts (the explore path and the multi-explore path) now append the dead Partner's attached cards to `removed` (the codebase's trash destination, same as MA-036 Reaper) and also clear partnerHp/partnerMaxHp, which were left at 0 as stale state. Regression tests: partnerLevel.test.ts section 7 (death removes the Partner, trashes the attached card, leaves the Main at full Health, the Main can still explore while leader:'partner' is refused) and ui.test.tsx ('falls back to the Main character once the Partner is gone'). Gates: game-core 840, client 184, server 102, typecheck clean, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T18:38:26", "task": "Fix freeze when all human seats are dead (bot-only endgame)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'while playing as pr-010, after being downed for the last time, my health reset to -10 and the game is frozen waiting for bot 2 (pr-009, both abilities)'. ROOT CAUSE: ws.ts advanceBots ran ONE bounded pass (<=2000 bot actions) after a human move and then stopped; with every human dead nothing ever re-triggered it, so the room sat on 'Waiting for Bot N...' forever. Reproduced at the ws level by driving the human to permanent defeat (revive at maxHp<=0) and watching the room go silent; engine sweep showed bot-only endgames routinely need >2000 actions (2084-5751) and ~half stall past 8000 (a bot at 1 HP never explores, so the game cannot end). FIX (server/src/ws.ts): advanceBots is now chunked - BOT_PASS_BUDGET=200 actions per pass (a yield point, not a stop), and when a pass ends on a bot's turn the stretch continues in background passes (50ms apart, one per room) that broadcast views as they go, so the client sees the endgame played out. BOT_ENDGAME_BUDGET=8000 caps the stretch; on the cap the match is concluded with the same Decorations-then-Health ranking checkWin uses and endReason 'allHumansDead' (HostResult union extended), so a stalled endgame costs bounded CPU instead of grinding forever. Client: SeatSwap shows 'Your character has fallen. The match is over.' for that reason instead of the inaccurate 'The Mansion is cleared'. NEW REGRESSION TEST server/src/botEndgame.test.ts: drives a deterministic-seed human to permanent defeat and asserts the room keeps producing stateSyncs after the death (verified to FAIL with the pre-fix stop restored). Gates: typecheck clean (all 3 workspaces), client 178, game-core 804, server 103."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T19:05:20", "task": "CORRECTION: bot-only endgame regression test details", "status": "ok", "note": "Addendum to the previous entry. The pre-fix freeze is CONFIRMED on seed 131 (correctly instrumented sweep: human permanently defeated at turn 496, then no gameOver and no further stateSyncs for 45s; the pre-fix pass had run its 2000-action cap and stopped). Two earlier debug sweeps reported false freezes because they broke on the death view and discarded the batch that could contain the gameOver - the same batching artefact that made the first version of the regression test fail for the wrong reason. FINAL TEST server/src/botEndgame.test.ts uses seed 131 with a new createGameServer test hook botEndgameBudget (default 8000 in production) set to 2500, scans every batch, and asserts (a) >=2 stateSyncs after the death and (b) a gameOver arrives. Verified: PASSES with the fix (~10s), FAILS with the pre-fix stop restored (0 views, no result, runs to the 90s deadline). Gates: typecheck clean, server 103, client 178, game-core 804."}
{"ts": "2026-11-09T22:50:00", "task": "Fix Sherry forced explore: engine no-op + client/server disagreement + reveal overlay", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: \"When sherry uses her ability to force another player to explore, nothing happens the reveal doesn't play\". THREE COUPLED CAUSES. (1) ENGINE NO-OP (engine/allyExplore.ts): resolveAllyExplore returned the state UNCHANGED when the combined arsenal was empty (if (weaponIds.length === 0) return state) and on insufficientAmmo. The card says Sherry FORCES the explore, so it must happen - unarmed if necessary. Removed the empty-arsenal early return; the insufficient case now selects the weapons that fit (cheapest first) via the new exported allyExploreUsedWeaponIds, and an empty arsenal is a valid result. (2) CLIENT/SERVER DISAGREEMENT (engine/validate.ts): forceAllyExploreWithSupport required Sherry to afford the TARGET's arsenal, but the client enumerates from its SANITIZED view (other seats' hands are hidden-*), so the ability button appeared and the server then rejected it (\"not enough Ammo to assist\"). Removed the hand-dependent Ammo precondition - the ability is offered whenever another living player exists, and the resolution spends what the combined Ammo can pay for. Regression test asserts enumerateLegalActions agrees between the full state and sanitize(state, 0). (3) REVEAL OVERLAY NEVER FIRED (client/src/ui/anims.ts + engine/actions.ts): a forced explore resolves through chooseOption, and detectReveal only accepted a literal explore action by the viewing seat. The reducer now appends an explore log entry (new optional Action.explore.forcedBy) so the overlay fires and the turn history shows the target's explore; detectReveal accepts it for the exploring seat OR the forcing seat, and MansionReveal reads \"Damage dealt\" for a viewer who is not the explorer. BROWSER-VERIFIED (server room, Sherry + bot): with 0 Ammo the ability opens the prompt, the bot explores with the combined 0-cost knives, and the overlay shows the Hunter, \"Damage dealt: 20\", the four knives and \"escaped to the bottom of the Mansion\"; the turn history reads \"Bot 2: explored the Mansion with Combat Knife x4\". Also verified with Ammo spent (Licker, \"Damage dealt: 15\"). Tests: engine/fanSherry.test.ts +3 (unarmed explore, forced-explore log entry, full-vs-sanitized enumeration), client/src/ui/anims.test.ts +3 (forced-explore reveal for explorer / forcer / unrelated seat). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), server 104, client 186, game-core 844."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T04:20:00", "task": "FCH-008 Sherry Birkin art re-pulled uncropped (whole card, not the 320x260 art window)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny sent a single-card image of Sherry Birkin (452x630 JPG) and said 'pull this art again, no cropping'. The existing CARD-ART/FCH-008.png was still the old 320x260 ART WINDOW (portrait only - no [CHARACTER] banner, no name bar, no ability text), the same crop the CH art used before it went full-card; every other character card (CH-*, PR-*) is now the whole-card scan. The new file is the WHOLE CARD at 320x446, quantized to 256 colours, 109,281 bytes. The source is trimmed exactly to the card's own border with no background (verified by reading the image: banner, portrait, name bar and ability text box all present, border visible on all four sides). Its ratio (0.7175) differs slightly from the character sheet's 320x456 (0.7018), so object-fit: contain letterboxes it by about 5px top and bottom; the Health badge measures (89.6%, 7.1%) against the standard .card-character geometry of (89.7%, 7.7%), so no badge override was needed. FCH-008 is the only FCH-* card with art - the rest of that character set has no sheet, so nothing else needed the same treatment. Verified: vite emits FCH-008-DHnWXYg8.png and :1724 serves it (109,281 bytes)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T04:32:00", "task": "CU-001 Ricardo Irving art re-pulled uncropped (whole card, not the 320x260 art window)", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny sent a single-card image of Ricardo Irving (569x800 JPG) and said 'update the card art for this one, do not crop'. The existing CARD-ART/CU-001.png was still the old 320x260 ART WINDOW (portrait only - no [CHARACTER] banner, no name bar, no ability text), the same crop the CH art used before it went full-card. The new file is the WHOLE CARD at 320x450, quantized to 256 colours, 97,049 bytes. The source is framed exactly to the card's edges with no background (verified by reading the image: light-green top border with [CHARACTER] and the 80 Health badge, portrait, tan text box with name + both level lines, copyright + CU-001 code line at the bottom). Caveat: the decorative gold flourish at the card's top-left is itself clipped by the LEFT edge of the source image - that is how the scan is, not something the extraction did. The Health badge measures about (88.8%, 8.4%) against the standard .card-character geometry of (89.7%, 7.7%), so no badge override was needed; the art's ratio (0.7111) differs slightly from 320x456 (0.7018), so object-fit: contain letterboxes it by about 3px top and bottom. cu-001 is a custom character defined in game-core/src/data/custom.ts. Verified: vite emits CU-001-DW3Utc3I.png and :1724 serves it (97,049 bytes)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T04:00:00", "task": "Poison becomes a single lobby check; 5 Blue Herbs; counter supply hidden until attached", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: \"Remove ex-006 through ex-009 from the custom card check list, replace it with a single check called poison; when selected add 2 x ex-006 and 2 x ex-008 to the mansion, add a stack of 5 blue herbs to the resource pile. The game board shouldn't show poison counters until they are attached to a character.\" THREE PIECES. (1) ONE LOBBY CHECK (client/src/ui/Lobby.tsx): EX-006..EX-009 are filtered out of the Custom Cards picker and replaced by a single POISON check; selecting it stores the option id \"poison\" in the room's customCards. (2) THE BUNDLE (game-core/src/data/cards.ts): new POISON_OPTION_ID, POISON_BUNDLE (ex-006/007/008/009) and expandCustomCards(), used by BOTH cardsForScenario and pilesForScenario so the server host and pass-and-play agree; EX-007's copies is now 5 so the bundle's custom-ex-007 pile is a 5-card stack (was 1); EX-009 is pulled in as the shared-supply counter the two Infected attach. (3) THE BOARD (client/src/ui/Board.tsx): the \"Counter supply\" pile renders only once at least one counter is attached to a Character (state.seats.some(s => (s.counters ?? []).length > 0)) instead of whenever the supply is non-empty. BROWSER-VERIFIED (server room, POISON selected): the picker lists EX-001..EX-005 plus POISON (no EX-006..009); the custom-ex-007 pile reads \"5 left\"; the Mansion is 42 (38 + 2x EX-006 + 2x EX-008); the Counter supply pile is absent until a counter attaches. Tests: engine/unofficialExpansion.test.ts +2 (bundle selection, bundle seeding), client/src/ui/ui.test.tsx +2 (Poison check replaces the four cards, supply hidden until attached). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 848, client 188, server 104."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T04:45:00", "task": "UI: 2px all-round shadow on health-gauge numbers + decoration cost before the star in the skill box", "status": "ok", "note": "Two small UI asks from Manny. 1) 2px shadow all round the number in every health gauge: `.health-ring-label` (the <text> inside every HealthRing - characters AND infected cards share the class, so one rule covers every gauge) now carries four directional text-shadows at 2px offset / 2px blur in rgba(0,0,0,0.85). Four shadows rather than one blurred one, because `0 0 2px` leaves the diagonals too thin to read as an outline. The shadow is pure CSS, so the class is the whole contract; HealthRing.test.tsx gained a test asserting <text class=\"health-ring-label\"> survives, since dropping it silently makes the number unreadable over art. 2) Decoration cost before the star emoji in the character hover card: .skill-box in CardView.tsx read `Lv{level}:star`; it now reads `Lv{level}:{gate}{star}` where gate is that tier's level1At/level2At. Most characters gate L1 at 0, so they read Lv1:0* - the 0 means 'active from the start', not a typo. The ui.test.tsx assertions that pinned the old strings were updated to the real gates (Chris 0/4, LK-001 1/8, CR-001 0/7, CC-001 2/5, CU-001 3/8, Leon 2/6, Krauser 1/7). Verified in the browser: the skill boxes rendered Lv1:2 / Lv2:4 / Lv1:2 / Lv2:6 and getComputedStyle on the gauge label returned the four 2px shadows. Gates: client 188, typecheck clean, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T01:20:00", "task": "Granted Explores can be spent in the SAME explore (multi-explore choice)", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: 'how does the player specify he wants to do more than one explore? ... when the player selects a weapon that gives a +1 or more explore, he should immediately be given the chance to use that explore, i.e. a player chooses to explore with a shotgun and nothing else, the player should have a choice to immediately use the second explore so when the mansion reveal happens two cards are revealed, or they can use that new explore later in the turn as a separate explore.' BEFORE: the action bar's 'Explores to use' selector was capped at the player's remaining Explores, so a Pump-Action Shotgun's +1 could only ever be saved for a later explore (the engine's exploreCount bound ignored the grant entirely). AFTER: (1) engine/explore.ts gains grantedExploresFor(weaponDefs) - sums grantExplores amounts (Pump-Action/Automatic/Riot/Triple Barreled Shotguns, Stun Rod) plus WE-040 Flashbang's grantExploreAndSuppressLowHpInfected; (2) validate.ts bounds exploreCount by exploresLeft + grantedExploresFor(weapons) - the pre-existing exploresLeft >= 1 gate stays, so a player with no Explores still cannot start an explore; (3) actions.ts uses the helper, and the reducer's exploresLeft + grantedExplores already adds the grant back after spending, so spending it in the same action nets to 0; (4) client/src/ui/explorePicker.ts adds exploreCountOptions(state, seat, weaponIds) (1..min(pool, mansion size)) and grantedExploresForSelection; ActionBar renders the selector plus a hint naming the granting weapon ('+1 Explore from Pump-Action Shotgun - use 2 to reveal that many cards now, or fewer to save some for later'); (5) ai/enumerate.ts offers 1 and the full pool so bots spend grants too. ALSO FIXED a latent multi-explore conservation bug this exposed: MA-092's 'Gain 1 copy' reveal gain was applied to fxState (a pre-gain seat snapshot) and then overwritten by newPlayer, leaving the copy registered in state.cards but in no zone (the full-game soak caught it as partnersInEscape/3 'registered instances in no zone: we-024#g1437-0-0'). mercenaries.ts gains gainCopyTracked() which reports the created ids; actions.ts carries them into the exploring seat's discard. Tests: engine/multiExplore.test.ts +5 (same-action spend, save-for-later, bound, enumeration, MA-092 conservation), client/src/ui/ui.test.tsx +2 (exploreCountOptions includes the grant, ActionBar hint). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 853, client 190, server 104."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T09:05:00", "task": "Rules: unarmed explore is legal; forced Explore always blocks endTurn", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny ruled: 'a player can technically explore if they have no weapons or ammo' (rulebook: 'plays all of their Weapons they will be using' - zero is a valid declaration). The forced-Explore obligation (Wesker L2 / MA-030 Cephalo) was silently lapsing whenever the target held no AFFORDABLE weapon, because canExploreLegally priced the seat's arsenal (hand weapon payable from turnAmmo) instead of asking whether exploring is possible at all. ENGINE: validate.ts canExploreLegally(state, seat) now returns true whenever the seat has an Explore left, the Mansion is non-empty, and a leader can field an explore (FCH-008 Sherry's cannotUseWeapons still excludes her, so she cannot be deadlocked either); downed/dead seats are excluded so a mid-turn downing cannot deadlock the guard. The explore action no longer rejects weapons: [] ('explore: no weapons' is gone). enumerate.ts starts the weapon-subset bitmask at 0, so the unarmed explore is in the action space and the UI offers it. POLICY: the bot never VOLUNTEERS an unarmed explore (0 damage, invites a hit) - chooseGreedyAction/choosePlayoutAction skip it unless player.mustExplore is set - and EXPLORE_BIAS no longer applies to it, so the endTurn pool-zeroing cannot make a weaponless bot gamble. It still plays one when a forced Explore blocks endTurn. CLIENT: evaluateExploreCombo checks the engine's legal set before the empty-selection hint, so the Explore button enables for an unarmed explore (default selection is still the fullest armed combo). VERIFIED by probe: forced + empty hand + 0 ammo -> bot buys then explores unarmed then endTurn becomes legal (trace: buy:am10 -> explore:0w -> endTurn(allowed)); not forced + empty hand -> endTurn. Tests updated: abilities (mustExplore deadlock test now asserts endTurn stays blocked with no weapon AND no ammo, and is allowed only at 0 explores), validate ('explore no weapons' -> legal), actions (unarmed explore no longer throws), enumerate (3 tests: 3->4, 0->1, 7->8 subsets), bot (action order 3->4 explores), policy (manualArgmax mirrors the skip), ui (data-combos 3->4). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 841 incl. soak, client 189, server 104. Soak natural-end rate 22/30 = 0.733 (floor 0.6) and the per-scenario rates are IDENTICAL to the pre-change HEAD (verified by git stash + re-run: alliance 0/3, partnersInEscape 1/3, outbreak 1/3 both before and after), so the expansion stalls are pre-existing balance, not this change."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T10:26:55", "task": "Leon L2 pistolsTwicePerTurn per official FAQ (double use in ONE explore)", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny quoted the Master FAQ (CH-002): 'When he uses a pistol weapon, you can pay its ammo requirement twice for that weapon to apply its effect and damage twice' and said the game did not do that - it only let a Pistol be REUSED in a later explore. Now ONE entry in an explore action's `weapons` array is one USE, so the same Pistol instance may appear twice in a SINGLE explore: requiredAmmoForExplore already sums per occurrence (ammo paid twice), the base damage is dealt twice, and every weaponEffects entry fires twice (grantExplores / gainCardsAndActions / plusDamagePerExtraWeapon / ...). The two uses may still be SPLIT across two explores (the old play-area reuse is kept), and the per-turn cap of 2 is enforced by the new canUseWeaponTimes helper - weaponUsesThisTurn now counts OCCURRENCES in the log, not log entries, so a double use spends both uses and a later explore is correctly rejected. Wiring: validate.ts (the 'explore: duplicate weapon' rejection became a per-weapon cap check -> 'explore: weapon already used: <id>'), actions.ts (new uniqueWeapons de-dupes freshWeapons / toTrashAfterUse so a weapon used twice is still ONE card in the play area / removed), enumerate.ts (offers one doubled variant per weapon subset so the bots AND the client's legalExplores can reach it), game-core/src/index.ts (exports canUseWeaponTimes), client/src/ui/explorePicker.ts (pure toggleWeaponDouble) and ActionBar.tsx (a 'x2' button on every weapon option with remainingUses >= 2; the row became div.explore-option > label + button). Spec SPEC_LEON_L2.md; tests new game-core/src/engine/leonL2.test.ts (11) + 3 in client ui.test.tsx. Gates: typecheck x3 clean, game-core 864 (incl. full-game soak), server 104, client 88, vite build OK. Soak natural-end rate 23/30 = 0.767 IDENTICAL with and without the change (measured both ways in-session: full suite with the change, and soak-only on the stashed pre-change HEAD via git stash -u + re-run), so no balance regression; the conservation assertion passes. Browser-checked the built client on :1724 (pass & play): the picker renders the new div>label rows cleanly. Noticed, NOT done (separate feature): SK-021 Weapon Master LV.3 (exploreDuplicateWeaponEffect) is armed as duplicateWeaponEffect but never consumed by the explore path - it duplicates only the EFFECT, not the damage, so it needs its own wiring."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T10:45:00", "task": "Mansion reveal: battle-line layout (character+Partner | weapons | revealed card) and multi-infected reveals animate one at a time", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: 'update the reveal mansion layout, add the player's character and partner card to the left of the weapons used, lead character in the right. When multiple infected are revealed animate them into the reveal screen one at a time.' BEFORE: the reveal panel was a narrow (340px) vertical stack - title, damage, 'Weapons used' row, the revealed card, result, Continue - with no character/Partner shown and only ONE revealed card ever reported. AFTER: (1) anims.ts gains detectReveals(prev, next, mySeat) returning EVERY card the viewing seat's newest explore revealed, in REVEAL ORDER (the pre-explore mansion deck order IS the reveal order; a WE-019 bottom reveal sorts after the top cards). detectReveal is now just its first element, so the single-card callers and the old tests keep working. A multi-explore, a CI-002 Crow chain and a MA-039/MA-072 event expansion all land in the same list. (2) MansionReveal renders a BATTLE LINE - .mansion-door-party (the exploring seat's character + Partner cards, art-only, with the LED tag on whichever one led the explore and its live HP ring) | .mansion-door-weapons (unchanged 'Weapons used' block, now capped at 200px so it wraps instead of stretching the row) | .mansion-door-card (the revealed card, 145px). New optional props party / index / total; the panel is 700px wide and wraps on narrow screens. (3) The multi-card step-through: .mansion-door-card carries key={def.id-index}, so advancing the queue REMOUNTS it and re-runs the new door-card-in entrance (translateX(-46px) scale(0.8) fade -> none, 0.35s). A '1 / 2' progress chip appears and the button reads NEXT until the last card, where it reads CONTINUE. (4) App.tsx holds revealQueue + revealIndex instead of a single reveal; the party is built from the explorer seat's characterInstanceId / partnerInstanceId plus the explore action's leader (default 'main'), and the queued pending-death screen still plays only after the LAST card is dismissed. VERIFIED LIVE in the browser (server room, First Timer): single reveal shows [Hunk card + LED] [Combat Knife] [Bui Kichwa] left-to-right; a Partner-Mode room shows [Hunk 65HP + LED] [Partner 70HP] [Combat Knife x2] [Mimicry Marcus]; a hotseat probe (window.__store, since reverted) drove a 2-explore unarmed explore and the overlay stepped 1/2 Cerberus -> NEXT -> 2/2 CONTINUE with the entrance animation re-running on the remount. Tests: anims.test.ts +2 (multi-explore order incl. a re-inserted card first, several defeated Infected top-card-first) and the old 'prefers a defeated over a re-inserted' case rewritten as the multi-card behaviour it actually became; ui.test.tsx +3 (party renders both characters with the leader marked, progress + NEXT, CONTINUE on the last card). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 853, server 104, client 195, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T12:10:00", "task": "Reveal overlay: non-Infected reveals show, their prompts render inside it, and the panel locks until they are resolved", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: 'Non infected cards should still trigger the mansion reveal screen, prompts caused by revealed non infected cards should display in the reveal mansion screen, the reveal screen should lock until all prompts are resolved.' BEFORE: a non-Infected reveal (item / token / event with a Take-or-Send-to-bottom choice) never opened the overlay at all. The engine REMOVES the revealed card from the mansion deck and parks it in NO zone while its takeOrBottom prompt is open, so detectReveals' zone diff could not see it (it only matched cards that moved mansion -> attached/mansionBottom/removed, plus re-inserted cards found back in the deck). AFTER: (1) anims.ts Reveal.outcomeZone gains 'pending', and detectReveals now also walks the revealed set (the top exploreCount of the PRE-explore deck) looking for a card that is in NO zone in the next state -- that is exactly a non-Infected reveal awaiting its prompt. Re-inserted cards still report 'mansion'; the zone diff still catches defeated/escaped/removed and the crow / MA-039 / MA-072 expansions that land beyond the top N. (2) MansionReveal gains prompts / state / onChooseOption props: pending prompts render as the prompt text plus its option buttons INSIDE the panel (the overlay would otherwise cover the ActionBar they used to live in), Continue is disabled, and a hint reads 'Answer the choice above to continue.' (3) App.tsx maps 'pending' to '<name> is revealed - answer the choice below to continue.' and passes the exploring seat's LIVE prompts plus a chooseOption dispatcher. The prompts are only offered when the VIEWER is the explorer, because the server rejects a chooseOption whose seat is not the sender's (host.ts: action.seat !== human.seat) -- a forced-explore watcher (FCH-008 Sherry) must not be shown buttons it cannot press. (4) promptLabels.ts is the prompt option-label helper extracted from ActionBar so both surfaces render identical labels; ActionBar now imports it. VERIFIED LIVE via a throwaway window.__store hotseat probe (reverted): exploring into the Rocket Launcher Case token opened the overlay with the token card, the 'Gain the Rocket Launcher weapon' prompt and TAKE / SEND TO BOTTOM OF MANSION inside the panel, Continue disabled (data-reveal-locked=true, lock hint shown); clicking TAKE granted the weapon to the discard, dropped state.prompts to 0 and re-enabled Continue (lock hint cleared). A second run with the Gatling Gun Case token was screenshot-verified. Tests: anims.test.ts +2 (a non-Infected limbo card is detected as 'pending'; it is reported AFTER the Infected it was revealed with, in reveal order), ui.test.tsx +2 (the prompt renders with data-reveal-prompts / option buttons / data-reveal-locked and the hint; Continue stays enabled and unlocked when the reveal opened no prompt). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 864, server 104, client 201, vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-10T12:48:49", "task": "EV-001 Zombie Grab: enforce the choose-damage-or-trash contract on EVERY reveal path", "status": "ok", "note": "Manny: 'the zombie grab event card is not behaving correctly, on reveal the player must choose between taking damage or trashing the card. Then it should be shuffled back into the mansion deck.' The single-explore direct reveal already did this (customZombieGrab.test.ts), but THREE other reveal paths skipped it: a multi-explore (exploreCount>1) offered ev-001 as a takeOrBottom Take/Send-to-bottom prompt (so 'Take' could dump the event into the player's hand), a CI-002 Crow chain silently shuffled it back with no choice at all, and MA-039/MA-072 expansion reveals shuffled/bottomed it. Fix: route ev-001 to its own zombieGrabIds list in the multi-explore classifier (checked BEFORE expansionIds so Crow/expansion reveals offer the choice), build zombieGrab prompts beside nonInfectedPrompts from handAfter+discardAfterExplosives, merge into the final prompts; intercept ev-001 as the second card in the MA-039 and MA-072 single-explore branches (park in limbo, prompt, resolver shuffles back); same intercept in allyExplore.ts (Sherry forced explore). Card text re-verified against CARD-ART/EV-001.png by two independent vision reads (cloud + local qwen3.5:9b): 'Trash a weapon from your hand or discard pile; otherwise, take 20 damage, then shuffle this card into the mansion.' Tests: 2 new cases in customZombieGrab.test.ts (8 total); full gate 866+104+201 green, typecheck 0 errors."}
