{"ts": "2026-11-10T13:50:00", "task": "Player area: Skill Area moved to the right of the character/partner cards", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny sent a screenshot of the player area and said 'i want to update the player area so that it behaves like this image, skills should be to the right of the players character/partner card'. BEFORE: the Mercenaries Skill Area was a horizontal wrapping strip in the footer dock, ABOVE the action bar (App.tsx rendered <SkillPanel> as a sibling of <ActionBar>), so it read as a separate band rather than part of the player's row. AFTER: (1) App.tsx no longer renders SkillPanel at all; (2) ActionBar.tsx renders it inside the action identity row as a new .action-col.action-col-skills immediately after the CharacterCards column, so the row is now character/partner cards -> Skill Area -> deck -> hand -> discard; (3) styles.css: .skill-panel becomes a vertical column (flex-direction: column, align-items: stretch, no card background / top rule) and .skill-panel .skill-row stacks label -> pips -> button so each slot reads as the tall dark panel in the reference. The vertical row rules are SCOPED to .skill-panel because .skill-row is shared with the character card's own skill list (CardView.tsx), which must stay horizontal. The panel renders null when the Skill System is off or the seat has no skills, so the column collapses to zero width. BROWSER-VERIFIED with a real pass-&-play game (Skill System on, full 5-round draft completed for both seats): the identity row measures character cards 80px -> SKILLS XP 0 column 110px (Extension LV.2 0/4, Medic LV.3 0/5, Luck LV.1 0/1) -> deck 76px -> hand 824px -> discard 76px, all bottom-aligned, and the skill slots render as vertical panels with a label, pips and an XP button. Test: client/src/ui/ActionBarPrompts.test.tsx +1 asserting the panel renders inside the identity row in that order (fails if it moves back to the dock). Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), client 202 passed."}
