{"ts": "2026-11-10T17:50:00", "task": "CR-001 missing its automatic +1 Buy on turn 1 (turn-start pools never applied to the opening turn)", "status": "ok", "attempts": 0, "note": "Manny: 'CR-001 dosent give the player it's automatic +1 buy each turn from it'S LEvel 1 ability'. ROOT CAUSE: startTurn is the only place the turn-start pools are applied (buysLeft = 1 + plusBuyBonus(seatAbils), Carlos goldAtTurnStart, Ada turnStartActionIfHpAtMost, Wesker forced Explore, skill ammo/gold) and the only place beginning-of-turn ability prompts are raised, but every caller (server/src/host.ts, client/src/hotseat.ts, ai/sim.ts) invokes it ONLY after endTurn while setup() returned the raw seat pools - so turn 1 ran on the setup values and silently ignored all of them. FIX: setup() now returns startTurn(baseState) on the non-skill path; the Skill System needed the same at the other entry into phase 'main', so advanceDraft returns startTurn(finishDraft(...)) when the draft completes (skill.ts imports startTurn from game.ts - safe cycle, both modules only use each other's exports inside functions). The opening state is now version 2, so 9 version assertions in game.test.ts / replay.test.ts were re-based +1. Tests: new engine/firstTurnStart.test.ts (4) - CR-001 turn-1 Buy, a character without the ability stays at 1, opening hand untouched, post-draft pools. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), client 202, server 104, game-core full suite green. BROWSER-VERIFIED over the real ws protocol (note: the dev server runs tsx with no watch and must be restarted after game-core edits - a stale server made this look still-broken): room 9W5UUN seat 0 = cr-001#1 buysLeft 2 turnNumber 1 version 2, client status bar reads BUYS 2."}
